      "final_disposition": "already-adapted",
      "decision": "The complete two-hunk patch guards both destruction-time removal of a manually bound modern click listener and touch-target focus before the input query exists. The owned legacy and untouched16 teardown never install/remove that modern listener;their cleanup stops FocusMonitor on the host ElementRef and invokes the initialized-or-noop selection cleanup. The current owned touch-target focus already has the optional input guard on both lines. Actual class execution covers destruction before init and after init/before view,cleanup order,missing/ready/disabled touch targets. Unsafe view dereferences and dropped cleanup are rejected. Both exact current peers now use a guarded Renderer cleanup closure and retain optional touch focus,including a modern disabledInteractive branch absent from the frozen legacy feature set. Do not import that modern lifecycle or feature. The prior rationale/note was incomplete or pre-adaptation;preserve it and replace it with this whole-hunk conclusion. Native creation/destruction and OnPush integration cases remain pending final Actions.",
